    "q-158011": {
      "dom_id": "step-q158011",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14274391/assets/a3dfc27c8cae5db8bccd14048366531e2aa556802943d464ea12b1568a8ba380.png)\n\nWhich of the diagrams shown above represent subspaces of ${R}^{2}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's analyze each diagram in turn.\n\n- Diagram I does not represent a subspace. The vector $a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ lies inside given subset. But\n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot a=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nlies outside the subset.\n\n- Diagram II does not represent a subspace. The vector $a=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ lies inside given subset. But\n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot a=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nlies outside the subset.\n\n- Diagram III does not represent a subspace since in does not contain the zero-vector.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"None\".",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
