      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14274391/assets/2739a0225640ff20cc9678edf8c41ba45ff637b17a40d0322ca792bef1346f06.png)\n\nWhich of the diagrams shown above represent subspaces of ${R}^{3}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's analyze each diagram in turn.\n\n- Diagram I does not represent a subspace. The origin $0=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ clearly lies outside the subset.\n\n- Diagram II does not represent a subspace. The origin $0=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ clearly lies outside the subset.\n\n- Diagram III represents a line passing through the origin. Therefore, it is a subspace of ${R}^{3}.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
